    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 in `AcceptanceTest`, the only test class).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional `postcode` to owners, validated per the fixed region table, keeping each changed unit small and isolated.\n\n**What I changed (6 files):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property (4-digit, documented range rules) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, the field appears in both the request DTO and the response DTO, and MapStruct maps it by name automatically \u2014 so it's stored and returned with no mapper changes.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 a `postcode` column plus a trivial getter/setter (no logic added to any existing method).\n\n3. **`ValidateOwnerPostcode.java`** (new, one small method) \u2014 the whole rule in one cohesive place: absent \u2192 pass through (backward-compatible); present \u2192 must be 4 digits and, for a city with a known region (reusing the existing `Locality` helper), within NSW 2000-2099 / VIC 3000-3099 / QLD 4000-4099; unknown region accepts any 4-digit code. Invalid \u2192 400 via the existing `MissingOwnerFieldsException` 400 pathway (no new exception/handler/escalation files).\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `validatePostcode` step right after `build`, so it runs against the built owner within the same transaction.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **6. `db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `postcode` column and the matching value to the positional seed inserts (the test DB uses `ddl-auto=none`; h2 uses `ddl-auto=update`, and per the repo's existing convention only the hsqldb scripts are kept in sync).\n\n**Low-impact choices:** no existing function bodies were modified (only new methods/steps added), the region\u2192range logic lives in one new single-method class, and I reused `Locality` and the existing 400 exception rather than adding new classes.",
